## 50,001 results is refused, not truncated

$ curl -sS -X POST localhost:8080/v1/runs --data-binary @toobig.json
{"error":{"code":"too_many_results","message":"a run envelope may carry at most 50000 results; chunk the run"}}
 (HTTP 413)

## The same POST under synchronous_commit=off (the M5.4 load-test profile),
## with the API restarted so the pool's sessions pick the setting up

$ psql -tAc 'show synchronous_commit'
off
$ time curl -sS -X POST localhost:8080/v1/runs --data-binary @big3.json   # fresh run_id
{"run_id":"99999999-aaaa-4bbb-8ccc-ffffffffffff","results":50000,"inserted":50000,"skipped":0,"duplicate":false,"machine_id":"7fea9ecafd05d7a64f0fcd74cf35f695"}
real 2.08 s

